infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title CTE vs VIEW: same SELECT, different lifetime
  desc A CTE's name dies with its statement; a view is stored in the catalog and reused across queries
  compares
    - label CTE — a named subquery in WITH
      children
        - label Lives for one statement
          desc The name vanishes the instant that statement finishes
        - label Within-statement reuse
          desc Reference the name several times in the same query, no duplicated text
        - label Not a stored object
          desc Nothing in the catalog; debug each step by running its SELECT alone
        - label Best for: a readable one-off query
          desc Flatten a nested report into a top-down pipeline of named steps
    - label VIEW — a stored named query
      children
        - label Persists in the catalog
          desc A stored object that outlives any single statement, until you DROP it
        - label Cross-statement reuse
          desc Any query, any time, can SELECT from it by name
        - label A catalog object
          desc Lives in the schema as reusable, named query logic
        - label Best for: shared query logic
          desc The same named query reused across many separate statements
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
